  "raw_text": "22\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh68\n):\n \nLasarus ra rait karna klubi alkan kaia sa\n \n–\n \n(They) must have given Lasarus a really big embrace\n \n/\n\n(Ellos) deben haber dado a Lasarus un abrazo realmente grande\n)\n\nMahka alki daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto apply immediately, to put into practice immediately\n \n/\n \naplicar de inmediato,\n\nponer en práctica de inmediato\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n12/18\n):\n \nSaulo witin\n \ndîa lan\n \ntakan ba mahka alki daukan.\n \n–\n \nWhat Saul\n \nlearned, he put into practice\n\nright away\n.\n \n/\n \nLo que Saúl aprendió, lo puso en práctica de inmediato.\n)\n\nWali alki daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto listen in order to apply, to listen in order to put into practice\n \n/\n \nescuchar para\n\naplicar, escuchar para poner en\n \npráctica\n\nAlki mangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto get/take/catch, to put/place\n \n/ obtener, tomar, atrapar, poner, colocar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb38\n):\n \nYawan alki silak ra mangkaia want sa\n \n–\n \nWe want to catch him and put him in jail\n \n/ Queremos atraparlo y\nmeterlo en la cárcel)\n\nAlki priskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto catch and take captive, to catch and tie up, to catch and take into custody\n \n/ atrapar y llevar\ncautivo, atrapar y atar, atrapar y poner bajo custodia\n\nAlki saura munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto abuse\n \n/ abusar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nRau sauhkanka wahwaia\n)\n\n(Note/Nota: This term can be used to refer to sexual abuse / Este término puede usarse para referirse al abuso sexual)\n\nAlki saura mamunra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nabuser\n \n/ abusador\n\nAlki saura munaia ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nabuse\n \n/ abuso\n\nAlki takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto hold back, to keep back, to detain, to hinder, to control\n \n/ retener, contener, detener,\nobstaculizar, controlar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb84\n):\n \nJisas pâsa bara lî alki takaskaia sip kan\n \n–\n \nJesus was able to control the wind and the rain\n \n/ Jesús pudo\ncontrolar el viento y la lluvia)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n \n(\nmwb-05/22\n):\n \nWan brinka nani alki takaskaia dukiara, Jehova ra bik takaia sa ai hilpka wankbia.\n \n–\n \nIn order to\ncontrol our desires, we must beg Jehovah to give us his help.\n \n/ Para controlar nuestros deseos, debemos suplicar a Jehová\nque nos dé su ayuda.)\n\nAi wîna alki takaskan lâka ba briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have self-control over their body, to have control over\nthemselves\n \n/ tener autocontrol sobre su cuerpo, tener control sobre sí mismos\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-05/20\n):\n \nJosep ba ai muihnika nani ra kaikan taim, ai wîna alki takaskan lâka ba brin.\n \n–\n \nWhen Joseph\nsaw his brothers, he had control over himself.\n \n/ Cuando José vio a sus hermanos, tenía control sobre sí mismo.)\n\nAlki takaskras\n \n(v-neg)\n \n–\n \nnot hold back, not keep back, not detain, not hinder, not control\n \n/ no retener, no\ncontener, no detener, no obstaculizar, no controlar\n\nKupia alki takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto control (the) heart, to have self-control, to deal patiently with someone or\nsomething\n \n/ controlar (el) corazón, tener autocontrol, tratar pacientemente con alguien o algo\n\nKupia alki takaskan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nself-control, control of the heart, to have control of the heart\n \n/\nautocontrol, control del corazón, tener control del corazón, autodominio\n \n(See also/ Ver\ntambién:\n \nWîna alki takaskan lâka\n)\n\nTwisa alki takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto control the tongue\n \n/ controlar la lengua\n\nWîna alki takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto control the body, to control oneself\n \n/ controlar el cuerpo, controlarse a uno\nmismo\n\nWan wîna alki takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto control our body, to control ourselves\n \n/ controlar nuestro cuerpo,\ncontrolarnos a nosotros mismos\n\nWîna alki takaskan lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nWîna alki takaskaia lâka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncontrol of the body, self-control\n \n/\ncontrol del cuerpo, autodominio\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nKupia alki takaskan lâka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/21\n):\n \nKristian nani sut ba rum diaia dukiara wîna alki takaskaia lâka ba praptis munaia nit\nsa\n \n–\n \nAll Christians need to exercise self-control with regards to drinking alcohol\n \n/ Todos los cristianos\ndeben ejercer el autocontrol con respecto al consumo de alcohol)\n\nAlks\n \n(\nv\n-\nimp)\n \n–\n \ntake\n, get, hold, obtain, catch\n \n/\n \ntom\na\n,\n \ntome, tomen,\n \nobt\né\nn,\n \nobten\nga\n,\n \nobtengan,\n \nsoste\nn,\n \nsosten\nga\n,\n\nsostengan, consigue,\n \nconsiga\n,\n \nconsigan,\n \natrapa,\n \natrap\ne\n, atrapen\n\nBliki alkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nchasing to catch\n \n/\n \npersiguiendo para atrapar\n\nDutki alkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto hold tightly, to hold strongly\n \n/ sostener con fuerza, mantener fuerte\n\nInska alkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto catch a fish, to fish\n \n/ pescar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-11/18\n):\n \nJisas pruan ningkara, Pita bara disaipil wala nani ba inska alkaia wan\n \n–\n \nAfter Jesus died, Peter and the\nother disciples went to catch fish\n \n/ Después de que Jesús murió, Pedro y los otros discípulos fueron a pescar)\n\nInska âialkra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nfisherman\n \n/ pescador\n\nInska alkaia warkka ba\n \n–\n \nthe work of catching fish\n \n/ el trabajo de pescar, la pesca",
